-- R8: a defaulted section binder is filled in once, at the root.
--
-- Nothing has to supply `the rate`. When nothing does, every rule that reads it
-- sees the default, and sees the SAME value -- the default is one shared
-- definition, not a copy per reader. An explicit WITH overrides it for that
-- call and everything under it.

§ `Rates`
    GIVEN `the rate` IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 3

GIVETH A NUMBER
doubled MEANS `the rate` TIMES 2

GIVETH A NUMBER
tripled MEANS `the rate` TIMES 3

GIVETH A NUMBER
`both readers agree` MEANS (doubled TIMES 3) MINUS (tripled TIMES 2)

#EVAL doubled
#EVAL doubled WITH `the rate` IS 5
#EVAL `both readers agree`

#ASSERT doubled EQUALS 6
#ASSERT (doubled WITH `the rate` IS 5) EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `both readers agree` EQUALS 0
